# Skills shipped to the SDK at install time.
# CMake reads this list and copies each named file from skills/ to the SDK
# under <DAS_INSTALL_DOCDIR>/skills/. Single source of truth: top-level skills/.
# Edit this list when adding a user-facing (vs repo-internal) skill.
#
# INVARIANT: if a skill on this list references `skills/<other>.md`, that other
# skill must be on the list too, or the SDK ships a dangling link. The llvm_tune /
# perf_lint / style_lint entries below are here for exactly that reason
# (cross-referenced from daspkg, das_macros, and strings).
#
# The invariant cuts both ways, and the second direction is usually the right one:
# a skill that is not the SDK reader's concern stays OFF this list, and any shipped
# skill pointing at it says `repo-only` instead. That is why tutorials.md,
# documentation_rst.md, tests_in_repo.md and aot_testing.md are absent -- the last
# is the daslang repo's AOT test harness (test_aot, tests/aot registration,
# libDaScriptAot regen), which an SDK user has no way to act on.
#
# Keep this file ASCII-only, comments included: CMake's file(STRINGS) treats
# non-ASCII bytes as separators, so an em-dash inside a comment splits the line
# and the tail gets read as a skill filename.
clargs_usage.md
cpp_integration.md
das_formatting.md
das_macros.md
dashv.md
daslang_live.md
daslib_modules.md
daspkg.md
